      trivia: "【A Journey Across Three Origins】Cuban craftsmanship crossed to the Canary Islands, and from there to the Dominican Republic — Don Diego’s path mirrors in miniature the tectonic shifts of the cigar industry in the later twentieth century. 【Bearing a Kingly Title】The “Don” of the name is an honorific for men of distinction, and its dignified ring is inseparable from the brand’s philosophy of competing not on strength but on gentleness. A classic called the “King of Mild” for over half a century, it is quietly loved still as the after-dinner or morning cigar."
