      trivia: "The line name “The Banker”, and its format names Currency, Annuity, Arbitrage and Day Trader, derive from the founder Hermann Upmann’s trade as a banker. The conceit is that the special cigars he kept in his vault for his most important clients have been recreated in the Dominican Republic 170 years on. And as a result of Imperial Brands’ two-way split of the business in 2020, an intricate configuration arose in which Altadis USA, seller of the non-Cuban H. Upmann (on the Gemstone side), the La Romana factory that makes it, and the 50 per cent of Habanos S.A. that sells the Cuban version (both on the Allied Cigar side) were placed under separate capital — and the American sanctions of 2025 struck this configuration head-on, halting shipments to the United States for a time."
