      trivia: "MATASA, as the story is handed down, began in 1974 with “a hundred dollars, one chair and one telephone”, and the first two brands it made were Cubita and Fonseca. The white tissue wrapping of each individual cigar, the brand’s very byword, is held to be a device the founder Francisco E. Fonseca adopted to protect the wrapper, and it was carried on by the Cuban and non-Cuban versions alike — which means this feature is of no use in telling the two apart. The sale negotiations of December 2019 began between Janny García of My Father and Patricia Quesada, in charge of Quesada’s overseas sales — the daughters of two cigar families."
